2. Description of the Software
The Quotidian Vault is a portable file encryption utility. It leverages the .7z archiving engine combined with AES-256 encryption to compress and seal user data into a local cryptographic environment.
Local Execution: The encryption and decryption functions operate entirely on your local device.
Data Privacy: Unless you explicitly enable optional online features, the Software does not transmit your vault contents, passwords, or encryption keys to any external server.

3. Core Features & Mechanics
By using the Software, you acknowledge the functionality of the following core mechanics:
Custom Vault Explorer: A natively rendered graphical interface providing virtual folders, drag-and-drop encryption, and Smart Views directly in memory, bypassing raw archive structures.
Data Minimization & Portability: The Software is designed to run directly from a portable USB drive. Upon locking the vault or ejecting the drive, the Software is designed to minimize residual unencrypted data on the host system by securely removing temporary files after normal operation.
Auto-Scan Detection: The Software automatically detects hidden vaults on connected drives and mounts them securely.
Inactivity Safety Timeout: After 5 minutes of detected system inactivity, the Software will automatically trigger an emergency lock—purging unencrypted files from memory and firmly securing the vault.
The Danger Zone: Permanent, destructive actions (such as full decryption or vault deletion) are heavily restricted and require both the master password and your unique Recovery Code to proceed.

4. Local Key Management & Absolute Data Loss
The Quotidian Vault uses AES-256 local encryption. There are no backdoors, no cloud backups of your keys, and no "forgot password" mechanisms.
Credentials & Recovery: Accessing your vault requires your master password and your cryptographically secure Recovery Code (which can be exported as a PDF for safekeeping).
Irrecoverable Data: If you lose your master password and your exported Recovery Code PDF, your data is permanently lost. We do not possess master keys or recovery algorithms. The Mozzerella Company cannot recover lost passwords, decrypt data, or bypass the Danger Zone under any circumstances. You assume 100% of the responsibility for securely storing your passwords and Recovery Code PDFs.

5. Technical Risks and Software Limitations
While the Software utilizes robust AES-256 encryption, you acknowledge and accept the following inherent risks:
A. Host Machine Security
The Software encrypts data at rest. It cannot protect against compromised operating systems. The Software offers no protection against sophisticated forensic attacks, host-level malware, keyloggers, screen recording, spyware, or physical access by unauthorized individuals while your vault is unlocked.
B. Hardware Interruption & Archive Corruption
While the .7z architecture is highly stable, unexpected power loss, forceful ejection of a USB drive, or shutting down your computer during active encryption/decryption cycles could result in irreversible file corruption. You are solely responsible for safely ejecting hardware.
C. Vault File Deletion
Encryption prevents unauthorized parties from reading your files; it does not prevent them from deleting the vault container file itself from your hard drive or USB drive.
D. Backup Responsibility
You are solely responsible for maintaining adequate backups of your encrypted vaults and all data stored within them. Encryption is not a substitute for a comprehensive backup strategy.

